  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 229 PM EST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nCurrently-Tonight...Isolated to scattered showers and storms will \ncontinue through this evening (PoPs 20-40%), with greatest coverage \nfocusing inland or across west central Florida. However, some of \nthis activity will still be able to push onshore this afternoon into \ntonight. While amounts should mostly remain an inch or less, \nisolated higher totals up to 2-3\" will still be possible (mostly \nacross the interior). While floodwaters are slowly subsiding from \nthe excessive rainfall from the past couple of days, especially  \nacross southern Brevard County and the Treasure Coast, any \nadditional rainfall will only exacerbate ongoing flooding issues. \nA Flood Warning remains in effect for this area through tomorrow \nmorning, mainly to address the ongoing road closures and lingering\nflooding impacts. \n\nGusty winds this afternoon will diminish to 5-10 mph tonight, with \nmild overnight lows in the low to mid 70s.  \n\nWednesday-Friday...High pressure north of the area and offshore the \neastern U.S. coast will continue an onshore flow that will gradually \ndecrease through late week. Rain chances decrease to 20-30% \nWednesday and then mostly remain out of the forecast through late \nweek as drier air builds into the area. Highs remain above normal in \nthe mid 80s, with overnight lows dropping into the 60s as onshore \nflow weakens and drier air moves in.\n\nSaturday-Monday...A weak front will push through the area Saturday, \nwith conditions currently forecast to remain mostly dry through the \nweekend. A passing mid level S/W trough may lead to an increase in \nrain chances early next week, but model guidance is still not in the \nbest of agreement. For now, PoPs only rise to 20-30% on Monday. N/NW \nflow behind the front will lead to a gradual drop in temps, with \nhighs in the low to mid 80s on Saturday falling to the mid 70s to \nnear 80 degrees on Monday. Overnight lows are also forecast to \ndecrease from the 60s into the weekend, with upper 50s possible, \nmainly near to NW of I-4 into Monday night.",
